Section: Flying a VTOL
  On: desktop
  A [[VTOL]] takes off and lands straight up, like a copter, and flies forward on its wing,
  like a plane. The T1-S VTOL has two [[tilt-rotor]] motors on the wing and a third rotor in
  the tail. In a hover the two wing motors point up, and the three rotors hold the plane in
  the air. In forward flight the wing motors point forward and the wing lifts the plane. The
  change from one to the other is the [[transition]]. ArduPilot does it, and the console
  gives it the modes: the Q modes (QLOITER, QLAND) hover, and the normal modes (CRUISE) fly
  forward.

Background:
  Given the console is connected to a VTOL on the ground
